  "research_notes": "COLOR WORKFLOW: To change the color of an object, first select the object(s) with the Selection tool. On the left-hand properties panel, two color swatches will be visible: 'Stroke' and 'Background color'. Click the 'Stroke' swatch to open the color picker for the object's outline. Click the 'Background color' swatch to open the color picker for the object's fill. The color picker provides a palette of preset colors, a custom color option via hex code input, and a color picker (eyedropper) tool to sample a color from anywhere on the canvas. Select the desired color to apply it instantly. The same workflow applies to setting colors before drawing a new shape.\nGOTCHA: The standard selection box only selects objects that are *entirely* contained within it, not just touching it.\nGOTCHA: Clearing the canvas via the menu or shortcut (Ctrl+Delete) is permanent and cannot be undone with the Undo command.\nGOTCHA: When drawing shapes like rectangles or ellipses, holding Shift is required to maintain a 1:1 aspect ratio (to create a perfect square or circle).\nGOTCHA: Pasting an image from your clipboard can be done directly onto the canvas with Ctrl/Cmd+V.\nGOTCHA: Exiting the text editor requires pressing Escape or clicking outside the text box. Simply pressing Enter will create a new line.\nGOTCHA: Arrows will automatically snap and bind to the edges of other shapes. This can be helpful but may require careful positioning if you want to avoid it."
